QuestGuidance.Register("en",445,{
[14209]="70072EA2\n1\tDefeat Dwarf-wights (total: 8)\030Collect relics of Lâkindar (total: 4)\tYou have come to Lâkindar in search of relics from the mine's once-glorious past. The search would be easier if there were fewer wights about.\n2\tInvestigate the room at the end of the hall\tYou have collected what relics you could find in Lâkindar and spotted something strange. You should look into it.\n3\tExamine the tomb\tYou have collected what relics you could find in Lâkindar and have spotted a strange stone tomb. You should examine it.\n4\tDefeat the fell Temámir wight\tAfter collecting what relics you could find in Lâkindar, you spotted a strange stone tomb and awoke its resident.\n",
[14210]="70028E35\n1\tSpeak to Ash at Glân Vraig\tSpeak with Quartermaster Ash again and choose your reward for your continued efforts in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14211]="70029FAE\n1\tSpeak to War-tyrant Akúlhun at Gramsfoot\tSpeak with War-tyrant Akúlhun again to choose your reward for your continued efforts in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14212]="7002A60A\n1\tSpeak to Ash at Glân Vraig\tSpeak with Quartermaster Ash again and choose your reward for your continued efforts in the Ettenmoors.\n",
[14213]="70046898\n1\tRepair chest armour (total: 4)\030Repair boots (total: 4)\030Repair helmets (total: 4)\tChest armour, helmets, and boots that need repair are scattered around Aragorn's Pavilion, on the after-battle Pelennor. You should repair various armour pieces so that soldiers are well protected for the march east.\n2\tTalk to Angbor\tAngbor can be found at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor. You should talk to Angbor.\n",
[14214]="7004CE4B\n1\tInjured Elves can be found along the Forest River between Felegoth and Loeglond. You should heal injured Elves.\t\n2\tTalk to Lorndúr\tLorndúr can be found in Loeglond. You should talk to Lorndúr.\n",
[14215]="700379BF\n1\tThe mead hall of Woodhurst has become a scene of battle, like much of Rohan. Calin mentioned that there were members of Herubrand's family who did not return after the battle and are presumed dead. While searching for evidence you should try to determine their whereabouts.\t\n2\tThe mead hall of Woodhurst has become a scene of battle, like much of Rohan. Calin mentioned that there were members of Herubrand's family who did not return after the battle and are presumed dead. While searching for evidence you should try to determine their whereabouts.\t\n3\tTalk to Calin\tCalin awaits your return in the farmhouse with news of your investigation. You should let Calin know that you found where Heremond and Cynethryth fell.\n4\tFind the trap-door to Herubrand's hideout\tFind the trap-door behind the curtain and counter area in the back of the farmhouse room. The trap-door is a hidden door leading to Herubrand's hideout.\n5\tTalk to Herubrand\tHerubrand is barricaded in the cellar of the farmhouse. Calin suggested you tell Herubrand the news of his father and wife.\n",
[14216]="70041A4B\n1\tDefeat Half-trolls in Hata Kebir (total: 4)\030Burn rowing boats in Hata Kebir (total: 12)\030Defeat Corsairs and Haradrim in Hata Kebir (total: 12)\tHalf-trolls and men devoted to the Heirs of Castamir can be found in Hata Kebir in south-eastern Lebennin. Jajax has asked you to help him weaken the forces of the Heirs of Castamir before they can cause further harm to Umbar.\n2\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax can be found at your side or can be called with your horn. You have greatly weakened the forces of Hata Kebir and should now speak to Jajax.\n",
[14217]="70057851\n1\tFind Otgand the Vile\tFew have encountered Otgand the Vile and lived to tell the tale of him, but on one matter they all agree: you do not want to encounter Otgand.\n2\tDefeat Otgand\tFew have encountered Otgand the Vile and lived to tell the tale of this foul creature. Seek him out and end this scourge of Misthallow.\n3\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[14218]="7003EB03\n1\tDefeat crawlers in Nan Tornaeth (total: 10)\tThere are crawlers infesting Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws. While in Nan Tornaeth, you should purge as many of the foul flesh-eating crawlers infesting the ruins as you can.\n",
[14219]="70044D58\n1\tTalk to Gúldil\tGúldil can be found just inside the Old Archives in the tunnels of the Fifth Circle. Gúldil has asked you to confront the thief in the Old Archives.\n2\tTalk to Gúldil\tGúldil can be found just inside the Old Archives in the tunnels of the Fifth Circle. You have defeated the fell power summoned by the scroll and cleared the Archives of danger. You should now speak to Gúldil.\n3\tTalk to Maenir\tMaenir can be found on the first floor of the Houses of Lore in the Fifth Circle. You should inform Maenir that the scroll is destroyed and the fell power within it banished.\n4\tTalk to Mithrandir\tMithrandir is in the Court of the Fountain on the Seventh Circle of Minas Tirith. You should inform Mithrandir of what you encountered in the Old Archives.\n",
[14220]="70062928\n1\tTalk to Leri Grudd\tClegur can be found south-east of Mossward past the Howlingstones. You should ask Leri Grudd about the floating village.\n2\tFind Leri Grudd's family parcel\tLeri Grudd has given you exact instructions on where the parcel was buried. Find the parcel in the ruffian camp north of Clegur and return it to her.\n3\tTalk to Leri Grudd\tYou found Leri's parcel. You should take it back to Leri Grudd and confirm its authenticity.\n4\tTalk to Cranog Dambryn\tCranog Dambryn wanders along the banks of the river north-east of Clegur. You should find them if you want to find Glyn Helyg.\n5\tDefeat ruffians in Radlaw (total: 12)\tThe ruffian camp Radlaw can be found north of Clegur. Cranog Dambryn has asked you to teach them a lesson.\n6\tTalk to Cranog Dambryn\tYou managed to create some chaos inside Radlaw. You should talk to Cranog.\n7\tLocate the first trail marker\tCranog has told you to look for trail markers he left that lead to Glyn Helyg.\n8\tLocate the second trail marker\tCranog has told you to look for trail markers in order to locate Glyn Helyg.\n9\tLocate the third trail marker\tCranog has told you to look for trail markers in order to locate Glyn Helyg.\n10\tLocate the fourth trail marker\tCranog has told you to look for trail markers in order to locate Glyn Helyg.\n11\tDeliver Leri Grudd's parcel\tYou have found Glyn Helyg. You should deliver Leri's parcel to her cousin Gwenfor.\n",
[14221]="700604B1\n1\tTalk to Himeinior to the west, in Tornhad\tThe Ranger Himeinior stands to the west of the entrance of Tornhad.\n2\tDistribute rations among the provision crates in Tornhad (total: 10)\tThe Ranger Himeinior gave you a bag of rations to distribute throughout the encampment, asking you to fill up the provision crates found throughout Tornhad.\n3\tThe Ranger Himeinior gave you a bag of rations to distribute throughout the encampment, asking you to fill up the provision crates found throughout Tornhad.\t\n4\tTalk to Ravaedron in Tornhad\tRavaedron is speaking with the Rangers within the bounds of Tornhad.\n5\tTalk to Idhrenfair in Tornhad\tRanger Idhrenfair has caught your eye; he surely has a task of some kind for you to complete.\n6\tBring the swords awaiting repair to a barrel by the forge in Tornhad, to the south-west\tThe Ranger Idhrenfair gave you a number of swords that are in need of repair, and instructed you to leave them in a barrel near the forge for that purpose. The forge is to the south-west.\n7\tTalk to Prestadír by the forges in Tornhad\tThe Ranger Prestadír has a number of questions for you, and likely a task for you to perform as well.\n8\tThe Ranger Prestadír has asked you to conduct a patrol of the outskirts of Tornhad while he finishes up his work at the forge and speaks with Ravaedron.\t\n9\tTalk to Ravaedron in Tornhad\tRavaedron is in Tornhad, speaking with a number of the Rangers who dwell there.\n",
[14222]="70007F4A\n1\tDefeat goblins (total: 12)\030Defeat Blue-crag Chieftain\tThe Blue-crag Chieftain is at the large goblin camp in ruins to the south-west of Noglond. Embarrassed by his previous skepticism, Grímkell has asked you to raid the goblins in their camp and slay their chieftain. He suggested you take allies.\n2\tTalk to Grímkell Stonebearer\tGrímkell is in Noglond, north-east of the goblin encampment. You should return to Grímkell with news of your victory.\n",
[14223]="7006692C\n1\tDefeat vineyard flies (total: 7)\tMiruhir has asked you to defeat sickle-flies to the north-west of the vineyard. Defeat sickle-flies near Iáphel.\n2\tTalk to Miruhir\tYou should tell Miruhir that you have dealt with sickle-flies. Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.\n",
[14224]="70040046\n1\tDefeat bandits in their encampment\tBandits can be found in their encampment in the foothills of north-western Lamedon. You should defeat the bandits who attacked Fuirion.\n2\tDefeat violent bandits (total: 8)\tBandits can be found in their encampment in the foothills of north-western Lamedon. You should defeat the bandits who attacked Fuirion.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of the vicious bandits who so brutally attacked Fuirion, stealing his satchel and leaving him for dead.\n",
[14225]="7004041F\n1\tDefeat drunken Corsairs\tDrunken Corsairs can be found in the store-house of Lothgobel in central Lamedon. You should defeat drunken Corsairs.\n2\tDefeat drunken Corsairs (total: 6)\tDrunken Corsairs can be found in the store-house of Lothgobel in central Lamedon. You should defeat drunken Corsairs.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated several of the drunken Corsairs who took over the store-house in Lothgobel.\n",
[14226]="700005B1\n1\tSearch for Violet Underhill\tThe ruffians' camp is west of Bamfurlong. You must ford a stream at the top of a waterfall to enter the camp, which is set on the heights at Narrowcleeve. Farmer Maggot suggested you search the camp he told Violet about, just in case she went there alone.\n2\tFree Violet Underhill from the cart\tViolet Underhill is being held prisoner in a cart. Violet Underhill, against Farmer Maggot's warning, went to confront a camp of ruffians by herself. Now it is up to you to rescue her.\n3\tTalk to Mat Harfoot\tMat Harfoot can be found in Stock, outside The Golden Perch Inn. You should return to Stock and inform Mat Harfoot of Violet's release.\n",
[14227]="7000AC67\n1\tBring the viols to Maggie Smallwood\030Collect viols (total: 5)\tMaggie Smallwood is at the Bree Hunting Lodge, west of Bree's South-gate. Maggie Smallwood has asked you to craft viols for the woodworkers of Bree.\n",
[14228]="7005368B\n1\tYou may complete this quest at any time.\t\n",
[14229]="700536B6\n1\tYou may complete this quest at any time.\t\n",
